#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134218 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf29db1b-f47b-53de-b31d-e4da1d0a9e5f" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Triple Integral as a Mixed or Repeated Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "813acb01-54b2-523f-b6c1-8e9168914371" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x + z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131751} {:answer/id #uuid "fd1c8bc1-3201-5975-a643-c499e6e502b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131752} {:answer/id #uuid "234f294e-2580-53eb-91b4-3b4b0a28959b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131753} {:answer/id #uuid "2d97b16a-dff6-50b2-b990-0c53b4f98ce1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131754} {:answer/id #uuid "5006433b-41db-5c7e-9b9a-9b40093bcb33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131755}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "234f294e-2580-53eb-91b4-3b4b0a28959b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131753} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bfc79e7-c8e9-5c3c-a109-c8d47ef0c0d5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131750}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f9f2f2a5-47b5-5a66-9153-5085ab9c95cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-40503" :question/problem "$$\n{∭}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{∗}^{∗}{\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx\n$$\n\nThe triple integral above is defined over the type III region given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,-1\\le z\\le 2x+1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1+x+z}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "A type III region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,{u}_{1}(x,z)\\le y\\le {u}_{2}(x,z)}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type III region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063571/assets/0603bed12c6af74e46544d8bebc52362aed95a9a5ad7418ea4faaf228f3b5241.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type III region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,z)}^{{u}_{2}(x,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}(x,z)=0,\\,{u}_{2}(x,z)=1+x+z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n{∭}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{1+x+z}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,-1\\le z\\le 2x+1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by expressing the double integral over $D$ as a repeated integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{1+x+z}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2x+1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1+x+z}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dz\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{2x+1}{\\int }_{0}^{1+x+z}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b=(-1)+(2x+1)=2x.\n$$"}]}
